SUMMARY:[Hike - Intermediate] 10Km Fast Pace - Heber Down - Whitby
DESCRIPTION:GTA Hiking & Stuff\nHeber Down Conservation!\n\nThis is a **fa
 st-paced** intermediate hike (**Going between 4.5-5km/hr**) with few stops
 . The beginning will be flat with the paved sections\, and we will be goin
 g into the back trails\, where there will be mud. We will cover about 10km
  in 2 hours\, **with minimal breaks**.\n\n**Not a beginner hike!**\n\n**TH
 IS HIKE STARTS AT 9:05am**\n\nBring a water bottle and dress for the weath
 er.\n\nParts of the trail can get muddy from the snow melting. Be prepared
 .\n\nWe are going to meet at the Old Cullen Gardens parking lot.\nIntersec
 tion Cochrane & Taunton.\n\nGo to the back of the parking lot near the new
  Pickleball courts. The path starts to the left of the picnic shelter.\n\n
 **Hike leaves promptly at 9:05am**\n\n**LEGAL DISCLAIMER AND LIABILITY INF
 ORMATION:**\n\nBy RSVP'ing and paying the event fee (if applicable)\, you 
 are confirming that you have read\, understand and accept the following:\n
 \n1. **GTA Hiking Meetup is a private group**. Attending events is volunta
 ry by you as a member. Participation in any activity with us is at your ow
 n risk.\n2. By joining this event as a member you agree to indemnify and h
 old harmless its organizers\, co-organizers\, assistant organizers\, event
  hosts\, and other members from all claims or liability of every type (inc
 luding court costs and legal fees) for injury or death to any person or fo
 r damage to property\, loss of personal property or any other wrongful act
  arising out of or relating to your participation as a member. This agreem
 ent applies to you and to other persons (as your guests) who may accompany
  you in these endeavors.\n3. You also agree to hold the organizers as well
  as other group members harmless. By participating voluntarily in the grou
 p\, you expressly waive any and all such claims against each and every oth
 er member in the group\, including without limitation any and all claims a
 gainst the group organizer\, co-organizers\, assistant organizers\, and ev
 ent hosts.
