SUMMARY:Creating Habits of Self-Care and Environmental Care
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260414T213000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260414T223000Z
UID:69c837b64dacf581ff84fc41@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn about “soft self-discipline” and how this practice c
 an help with supporting ourselves in times of stress or with addressing ec
 o-anxiety.\nThis interactive workshop introduces participants on how to s
 tart journaling and how to use this to track your goals and habits. Track
 ing your habits is a self-care practice that can help connect you to the 
 natural world and the cycles of the seasons and life.\nPlease register onl
 ine.\nPresented by\nClementina Consens\n\, TPL's Spring 2026\nEnvironmenta
 list in Residence.\nThe Environmentalist in Residence\nis part of TPL's\nO
 ur Fragile Planet\nprogram series\, supported by Friends of Toronto Public
  Library\, South Chapter.​\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal
  information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under
  the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The inform
 ation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and 
 evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can b
 e directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 78
 9 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Malvern\, Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c837b64dacf581ff84fc41
