X-SOURCE-ID:toronto_festivals
SUMMARY:Pelléas et Mélisande
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260415T193000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260420T143000
UID:be17fc2d0aaae01a0fd68afd1fdc2828@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:Rich with symbolism and dream imagery\, Pelléas et Mélisande
  is Debussy’s sole opera\, and this uniquely imagined production has lon
 g been a dream of Co-Artistic Directors Marshall Pynkoski and Jeannette La
 jeunesse Zingg. \n\nBased on the symbolist play by Maurice Maeterlinck\, P
 elléas et Mélisande follows a prince lost in a forest who discovers a be
 autiful woman weeping beside a pool of water which brings him in contact w
 ith a supernatural world from which there is no escape. \n\nAssociate Musi
 c Director Dr. Christopher Bagan enthusiastically embraced the opportunity
  to realize a unique score of Debussy’s massive opera in a new arrangeme
 nt for Opera Atelier and 14 elite soloists from Tafelmusik Baroque Orchest
 ra. \n\nPelléas et Mélisande will feature David Fallis conducting and wi
 ll be directed by Marshall Pynko.\nCategories: Dance\, Live Performances\,
  Music
LOCATION:TELUS Centre for Performance and Learning at Koerner Hall\, 273 B
 loor St W\, Toronto\, ON\, M5S 1W2
URL:https://www.operaatelier.com/shows/pelleas-et-melisande/
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
