SUMMARY:Learn to Make a Video Game
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260416T220000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260417T000000Z
UID:69b309bb81b67dfe32ac20c5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn to make a 2D Platformer using the free browser-based vid
 eo game development tool : Construct 3\nLearn the basics of video game dev
 elopment using Construct 3\, a free browser-based game engine. In this ses
 sion you'll learn how to create a 2D platformer without the need for codin
 g. Participants will learn the interface and tools of the software\, and b
 y the end of the class will have built their own simple game.\nRegistratio
 n is required.\nRegistration begins on April 7th at 12:30pm.\nNote: Your s
 pot will not be guaranteed after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nI
 nformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is co
 llected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sec
 tions 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for eve
 nt and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how
  the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff 
 at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W
  2G8
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor - eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b309bb81b67dfe32ac20c5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
