SUMMARY:Robotics Night
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260422T220000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260422T230000Z
UID:69c6c9f8b6c4ac1fedc88fb5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for fun challenges with Dash robots using building & c
 raft materials and block coding.\nWed. Apr. 22                Twister with
  Dash\nWed. May 20                Explore Sphero\nWed. June 17            
     Make a ‘Pizza’ with Dash\n*Due to the limited number of robots\, p
 articipants may need to share a robot with other participants.\nInformatio
 n Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected b
 y the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(
 a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and pr
 ogram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the libr
 ary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswe
 rline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Barbara Frum\, 3rd Floor\, Room A
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c6c9f8b6c4ac1fedc88fb5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ab2b5d6724c63d00f732cf"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Photo Editing with Photoshop
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260422T220000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260422T233000Z
UID:69ab2b5d6724c63d00f732cf@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Adobe Photoshop is the world’s best imaging and graphic desi
 gn software and is at the core of just about every creative project\, from
  photo editing and compositing to digital painting\, animation\, and graph
 ic design.\nJoin us for an introductory lesson and learn about the most co
 mmon tools. We'll explore the workspace and enhance images while investiga
 ting tools such as crop\, levels\, colour balance and more. See how an ima
 ge can be altered and repaired using patch tools such as the clone and hea
 ling brush tools. We'll also dive deep into the world of layers and how yo
 u can manage them for those really unique and fun projects.\nRegistration 
 is required.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on 
 this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libr
 aries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only 
 be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Ques
 tions about how the library handles your information can be directed to An
 swerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\,
  Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:New Toronto\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ab2b5d6724c63d00f732cf
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69bb1da31e64afd01e6331c3"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Coding with Python
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260422T220000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260422T230000Z
UID:69bb1da31e64afd01e6331c3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Python is an open source programming language that is used for
  creating web applications\, web content\, mathematics and system scriptin
 g. In this course you will learn how python code works and given time to p
 ractice. Prior coding knowledge is not necessary for this introductory cla
 ss. Key takeaways will include a working knowledge of variables\, loops\, 
 conditional arguments and more.\nClass will utilize\njdoodle.com\nweb app.
  No account is required to use this site. If you are bringing your own dev
 ice please ensure it can connect to wifi.\nRegistration is required.\nInfo
 rmation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is colle
 cted by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sectio
 ns 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event 
 and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how th
 e library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\
 nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G
 8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, 1st Floor\, Learning Center 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69bb1da31e64afd01e6331c3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
