DESCRIPTION:One of the most accomplished violinists of her generation\, Li
 sa Batiashvili performs works by Beethoven\, Bartók\, Franck\, and fellow
  Georgian Ioseb Bardanashvili\, with her compatriot\, pianist Giorgi Gigas
 hvili.\n\nDescribed by The Times as “the complete musician\,” Batiashv
 ili commands her place among the world’s foremost artists with performan
 ces of great insight and expressive eloquence. The German-based violinist\
 , named Musical America’s 2015 Instrumentalist of the Year and also stan
 ds among the winners of Italy’s prestigious International Accademia Musi
 cale Chigiana Prize. \n\nBorn in Tbilisi in 2000\, Gigashvili’s musical 
 career took a decisive turn in April 2019 when he won First Prize at the V
 igo International Piano Competition.\n\nPlease join us! This concert is pr
 eceded by a short performance by talented students of The Royal Conservato
 ry. \n\nCategories: Arts/Exhibits\, Live Performances\, Music
LOCATION:Koerner Hall\, Royal Conservatory of Music\, 273 Bloor St W\, Tor
 onto\, ON\, M5S 1W2
