X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Botanical Garden": "https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/colourful-cacti-and-succulents-flowers-spine-and-leaf/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:toronto_botanical
X-SOURCE:Toronto Botanical Garden
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260430T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260430T193000
DTSTAMP:20260411T100103
CREATED:20260311T195537Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260311T195822Z
UID:10001949-1777572000-1777577400@torontobotanicalgarden.ca
SUMMARY:Colourful Cacti and Succulents: Flowers\, Spine\, and Leaf
DESCRIPTION:Calling all of the plant moms and dads\, the biophilia fans\, and the design junkies!\n \nTag along with Jess Conley (TBG Horticulturist) as she demoes how to create a FLOWERING\, low-water\, year round\, COLOURFUL\, Cacti and Succulent living arrangement. Tapping into her past in floristry and design\, she’ll teach you industry secrets to make your container arrangements pop\, draw the eye\, and flower floriferously.\n \nDesigning with colour for maximum impact\, marrying design strategies and horticultural know-how\, to get the most ornamental value. These types of arrangements\, if done properly will last many years and function as living art.\n \nThe demo planter will be going home with one lucky attendee!\n \nThursday\, April 30\, 6 to 7:30 p.m.Public $20\, TBG Members $15 (plus applicable taxes and fees).\n \nAbout Jess Conley\nJess Conley is a botanic jack-of-all-trades. She’s been a tree planter\, a florist\, an urban farmer\, and an estate gardener. She studied Landscape Design\, but she found her joy in tending life. One of her specialties\, amongst many\, is edible flowers. However\, her palate is not limited to just flowers\, she can often be found on the grounds sampling horticultural treasures such as maple samaras and paw-paw fruit.\nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden\nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member!\nAdditional Program Information\n\n\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program please email programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/colourful-cacti-and-succulents-flowers-spine-and-leaf/
LOCATION:Toronto Botanical Garden\, 777 Lawrence Ave E\, Toronto\, ON\, M3C 1P2\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Gardening
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/2c301b523560b05bee35eb54facd7900.jpg
END:VEVENT
