SUMMARY: New Music for Old Hands Concert Series: Adam Scime
DESCRIPTION:Matinee concert series at Labdara Lithuanian Nursing Home. Ea
 ch concert in this series will premiere a composition performed by the La
 bdara bell choir and Laura Gillis (conductor/pianist). Each composer will
  give a talk and share music with the residents and audience members\, fo
 llowed by a casual social mixer.\n\n2:00pm start time. Free Admission. Re
 serve your spot at Eventbrite. Limited seating available.\n\nMay 2: Adam 
 Scime\n\nAdam is a composer and performer\, and works as a leader in the 
 arts non-profit sector. He is currently the Executive Director of The Nia
 gara Symphony and Music Director of FAWN Opera in Toronto. Adam will talk
  about his approach to music and sound and play some examples of how he a
 pproaches sound in his music on the piano. The Labdara bell choir and Lau
 ra Gillis (conductor/pianist) will premiere Adam's piece\, Morning Rain.\
 n\nMay 16: Louise Campbell (joining us virtually from Montreal)\n\nMay 30
 : Lieke van der Voort (joining us virtually from Germany)\n\nJune 13: Ale
 x Eddington\n\nJune 20: Martin van de Ven\n\nwww.facebook.com/NewMusicFor
 OldHands http://www.facebook.com/NewMusicForOldHands
CATEGORIES:Music,Concert,#poweredbyTAC,#BringingTheArtsToLife
