SUMMARY:Therapy Dog Visits
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260507T194500Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260507T204500Z
UID:69b2e1f71e64afd01e619f4b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for visits with a therapy dog. Children will have an o
 pportunity to read\, listen to stories\, and engage in therapeutic human-a
 nimal interaction.   Children who live with a disability\, are neurodiverg
 ent\, or have experienced medical or other types of trauma are especially 
 welcome.\nThis program is presented in partnership with One Health Partner
 s.\nDrop-in\, no registration required.
LOCATION:Runnymede\, Children's Area
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b2e1f71e64afd01e619f4b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a0c4abcbf6405d3568bdad"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Teen Quiet Study
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260507T200000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260507T230000Z
UID:69a0c4abcbf6405d3568bdad@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you looking for a quiet space to study after school? Join 
 our quiet study hall at Locke's program room every Thursday for individual
  or group study. Tables and chairs are provided\, as well as a variety of
  materials to take study breaks.\nThis is a drop-in program for Teens\, a
 nd space is limited.
LOCATION:Locke\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a0c4abcbf6405d3568bdad
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
