SUMMARY:Hilary Hahn on Violin with Tom Poster on Piano
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260521T190000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260521T190000
UID:0e87ba8b1056cea73f880aee8428bd9e@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:Three-time Grammy Award-winning violinist Hilary Hahn melds ex
 pressive musicality and technical expertise with a diverse repertoire guid
 ed by artistic curiosity. She is currently artist-in-residence at both the
  Chicago Symphony Orchestra and London’s Wigmore Hall\, and is co-founde
 r and vice president of artistic partnerships of the AI-music initiative D
 eepmusic.AI. Hahn is a prolific and celebrated recording artist whose 21 f
 eature albums on Decca\, Deutsche Grammophon\, and Sony have all opened in
  the top ten of the Billboard charts.\n\nEnjoy her program of Maurice Rave
 l: Violin Sonata No. 2 in G Major\, M. 77\, Bun-Ching Lam: Solitude d’au
 tomne\, Lili Boulanger: Nocturne\, Maurice Ravel: Pièce en forme de Haban
 era\, M. 51\, Claude Debussy: Sonata for Violin and Piano in G Minor\, Sco
 tt Tixier: new duo work (North American premiere)\, and Gabriel Fauré: Vi
 olin Sonata No. 1 in A Major\, op. 13.\n\nCategories: Arts/Exhibits\, Live
  Performances\, Music
LOCATION:Koerner Hall\, Royal Conservatory of Music\, 273 Bloor St W\, Tor
 onto\, ON\, M5S 1W2
URL:https://www.rcmusic.com/events-and-performances/hilary-hahn
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
