SUMMARY:Introduction to 3D Printing
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260521T220000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260521T233000Z
UID:69cdb7e31e64afd01e665079@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn how 3D printers work and how you can print at the Toront
 o Public Library’s Digital Innovation Hubs. This class includes hands-on
  instruction with Prusa Slicer\, the software used to prepare your 3D obje
 ct file for printing on a Prusa MK3S+ 3D printer.\nDROP IN\nNote: Customer
 s are no longer required to attend a mandatory 3D printing class prior to 
 using a 3D printer at the Toronto Public Library’s Digital Innovation Hu
 bs. This class is for those who are interested in learning more about 3D p
 rinting and how to use the Prusa software.
LOCATION:Long Branch\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69cdb7e31e64afd01e665079
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69bc6cd08d5e2d0933667215"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Throwback Thursdays: Great Movies on the Big Screen
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260521T220000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260522T000000Z
UID:69bc6cd08d5e2d0933667215@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Come join us for a radical retro rewind projected on the big s
 creen. Whether you're a first-time viewer or long-time fan\, these movies 
 are sure to please.\nMarch 19: Michael Clayton (2007\, 14A)\nMarch 26: O
 cean’s Twelve (2004\, PG)\nApril 2: Bridesmaids (2011\, 14A)\nApril 9: A
 ustin Powers: International Man of Mystery (1997\, PG-13)\nApril 16: Meet 
 the Parents (2000\, PG)\nApril 23: Rounders (1998\, R)\nApril 30: No Count
 ry for Old Men (2007\, 18A)\nAll are welcome. Drop-in\, no registration re
 quired.
LOCATION:High Park\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69bc6cd08d5e2d0933667215
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
