SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Video Game Café
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260522T200000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260522T220000Z
UID:6971201c91e4576f847de1da@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us in the Youth Hub every Friday to play video games on o
 ur Nintendo Switch or PS5 with your friends! Ask us for our list of video 
 games\, and check our monthly calendar for Gaming Tournaments with prizes!
 \nThis program is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming pl
 ace for teens after school and in the summer\, where helpful staff are alw
 ays available. Free\, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a bra
 nch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to find out more.
LOCATION:Eatonville
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6971201c91e4576f847de1da
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b1b330403a4e5652dedb31"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Snap Circuits
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260522T200000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260522T210000Z
UID:69b1b330403a4e5652dedb31@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This month we will play with electricity and circuitry. Turn o
 n a light\, spin a motor\, activate a speaker and choose from hundreds of 
 different projects\, or try making your own circuits! For ages 6-12.\nRegi
 stration is required. Parent/Caregiver must attend.\nInformation Collectio
 n Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toron
 to Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\
 , and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regis
 tration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles
  your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.c
 a\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Spadina Road\, Canoe Table\, center of branch
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b1b330403a4e5652dedb31
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69612a7f6f926136000f424c"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/695fe14e4a9fd98b7f765ea3"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:After School Club
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260522T200000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260522T210000Z
UID:695fe14e4a9fd98b7f765ea3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Looking for something to do after school? Come out to our Afte
 r School Club and learn new things\, make stuff\, meet other kids and have
  fun!\nFor ages 6-12.\nRegistration is required.\nSnacks are offered durin
 g the After School Club for participants\, beginning at 3:45pm. Ingredient
  lists will be available. Snacks are generously supported\, in part\, by d
 onors.\nUpcoming Topics:\nMarch 6: Dash Robotics\nMarch 13: Collage Poste
 rs\nMarch 27: Games\nApril 10: Sphero Robotics\nApril 17: Planting Seeds
 \nApril 24: Snap Circuits\nMay 1: Crafts\nMay 8: Dash Robotics\nMay 15: 
 Beaded Wire Dragonflies\nMay 22: Marbled Paper\nMay 29: Sphero Robotics\nJ
 une 12: Melt Beads\nJune 19: After School Club Party\nInformation Collecti
 on Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toro
 nto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)
 \, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regi
 stration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handle
 s your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.
 ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Gerrard/Ashdale
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/695fe14e4a9fd98b7f765ea3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
