X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Board Game Café
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260526T200000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260526T220000Z
UID:69711d50992fc18a86deb18f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us in the Youth Hub every Tuesday to play board games wit
 h your friends! Ask us for our list of board games\, and check our monthly
  calendar for Tournaments with prizes! All materials provided.\nThis progr
 am is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teen
 s after school and in the summer\, where helpful staff are always availabl
 e. Free\, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a\n
 Youth Hub\nor call the branch to find out more.
LOCATION:Eatonville
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69711d50992fc18a86deb18f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69d116a41e64afd01e66e696"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Discovery Club: Dungeons and Dragons
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260526T200000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260526T210000Z
UID:69d116a41e64afd01e66e696@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn the basics of the popular fantasy role-playing game – 
 create your character and learn about game play including dice rolls\, sco
 ring\, and imagination! Meet your Dungeon Master and participate in a week
 ly fantasy campaign as your created character. Will you complete your ques
 t or get slayed by a vicious monster?\nThis program is for ages 10 to 14.
 \nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is
  collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, 
 sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for 
 event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about 
 how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline sta
 ff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON 
 M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Don Mills\, Lower level program room.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69d116a41e64afd01e66e696
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a8c194b48451fc3c06bf51"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Music and AI for Kids!
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260526T200000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260526T210000Z
UID:69a8c194b48451fc3c06bf51@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:For ages 8-12.\nJoin us for 4 weeks of goofy\, musical fun! Ou
 r Innovator in Residence\, Joel S. Silver\, will show you how AI works to 
 help you create music. Create songs with the silliest lyrics you can think
  of\, create a soundtrack for your own skits\, even write a theme song fo
 r the library! No music or computer experience needed - just bring your cr
 eativity!\nDrop-in. No registration required\, but space is limited.\nThis
  program is part of the Innovator in Residence (AI and Music Production) p
 rogram\, which is designed to help beginner and intermediate learners buil
 d knowledge and creative skills and get hands-on with current AI tools in 
 music production and learn about the history\, copyright and ethics of gen
 erative music. For more information and a full list of programs\, visit\nt
 pl.ca/airesident\n.
LOCATION:Fairview\, Room 201\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a8c194b48451fc3c06bf51
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/696fcdf91e64afd01e557b98"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:All Ages Karaoke and Board Game Night
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260526T213000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260526T233000Z
UID:696fcdf91e64afd01e557b98@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Come sing your favourite tunes on our stage in a fun\, encoura
 ging environment. Request any song and we'll try to find a karaoke video 
 and play it for you! If singing is not your thing\, a few board games will
  be on hand if you want to try out Catan\, Anomia\, Ticket to Ride\, or te
 st your vocabulary with Scrabble! You are also welcome to bring your own a
 nd invite others to play with you.\nChildren must be accompanied by an adu
 lt.
LOCATION:Palmerston\, Theatre (downstairs)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/696fcdf91e64afd01e557b98
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
