SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260411T140310Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260603T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260603T210000
SUMMARY:Koerner Hall:  2026 Griffin Poetry Prize Readings
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE\nWe attend the **Griffin Poetry Prize**
  every year!\n\n*A superb literary night of prose!*\n\nhttps://griffinpoet
 ryprize.com/\n\n*The Griffin Poetry Prize has been acknowledging and encou
 raging poets for twenty-two years. At a time when censorship and attacks o
 n a diverse array of writers are on the rise in many countries – includi
 ng the United States – it’s heartening to see such a strong vote of co
 nfidence in poets coming from Canada. Poetry is not a minor art form\; it 
 is the crucible of human language.*\n\nMargaret Atwood\, Founding Trustee\
 n\n**Tickets are $25 or $30\,** with the purchase link below. Tickets have
  just gone on sale. Includes a lovely WINE reception.\n\nAny seat is a gre
 at seat. I am sitting in Orchestra\, Row M.\n\nOn Wednesday June 3rd--\n\n
 The evening will include a selection of readings by some of the **world’
 s best poets\,** including the five poets shortlisted for the **$130\,000 
 Griffin Poetry Prize\,** this year’s Lifetime Recognition Award recipien
 t\, and the Canadian First Book Prize winner.\n\nIt will be a celebration 
 of poetry not to be missed! A harvester of words at the highest level. Lan
 guage artists!\n\nIf you've **not** attended before--take a chance this ye
 ar. You will experience nothing like it. This is our 8th year attending.\n
 \n**Ticket link--any seat is a great seat**\n\nhttps://www.rcmusic.com/eve
 nts-and-performances/2026-griffin-poetry-prize-readings\n\n\\-\\-\\-In 202
 3\\\, 2024\\\, 2025\\-\\-30\\+ of us attended each year\\. Your ticket als
 o **includes** an anthology of poems by short-listed authors (worth $20 at
  book shop)\, and some wine!\n\nNOTE: the 6:00 pm start time (wine recepti
 on/yummy snacks)\n\nPlan ahead so you can get there in time. Arrive by 630
 pm.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/toronto-arts-and-culture/events/31396
 6389/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260326T195023Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260326T195023Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
