SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Study Hall Wednesdays
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260603T200000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260603T220000Z
UID:69711e66992fc18a86deb255@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:On Wednesdays\, the Eatonville Youth Hub becomes a quiet space
  for teens to study\, work on projects\, and request homework help and res
 ume help from staff. Bring your homework and enjoy a snack in a space that
  is just for teens.\nThis program is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs
  are a welcoming place for teens after school and in the summer\, where he
 lpful staff are always available. Free\, nutritious snacks are offered da
 ily. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to find out m
 ore.
LOCATION:Eatonville
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69711e66992fc18a86deb255
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/694ac7789fb47cac989f34b9"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Parent/Child Graphic Novel Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260603T223000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260603T233000Z
UID:694ac7789fb47cac989f34b9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Share the love of reading as members of our book club for kids
  and parents! Read a book together\, then join us once a month at the libr
 ary to chat about the book. Was it a great read? Or a total stinker? All o
 pinions and thoughts are welcome and appreciated. For kids ages 9 to 12 an
 d their grown-ups.\nNo registration required. Copies will be available at 
 the front desk on a first-come\, first-served basis one month before each 
 meeting.
LOCATION:Runnymede\, 2nd Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/694ac7789fb47cac989f34b9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
