BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Botanical Garden": "https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/native-plant-series-potting-up-seedlings-plant-exchange/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:toronto_botanical
X-SOURCE:Toronto Botanical Garden
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260606T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260606T120000
DTSTAMP:20260411T100103
CREATED:20251205T182603Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20251222T174219Z
UID:10001898-1780740000-1780747200@torontobotanicalgarden.ca
SUMMARY:Native Plant Series: Potting Up Seedlings & Plant Exchange
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an engaging workshop series where you’ll learn about biodiversity\, native plants & how to enhance your garden! Nature needs your help\, and it’s as simple as using native plants in your garden! Biodiversity\, the variety of all living things necessary to sustain life\, is declining due to climate change\, habitat loss from increasing urbanization\, and agricultural practices. Discover the importance of native plants\, learn how to grow them to attract pollinators\, and enhance the beauty of your garden.\n \nSession 3: Potting Up Seedlings & Plant ExchangeGrow your gardening skills this winter with a hands-on seedling workshop! The Toronto Master Gardeners will demonstrate how to carefully select seedlings and pot them up into 4” pots\, giving you the confidence to nurture young plants at home. Participants in the January session are invited to bring their own germinated seeds to exchange with fellow gardeners\, while limited seedlings will also be provided for those who didn’t join the earlier sessions.\n \nSaturday\, June 6\, 10 a.m. to 12 p.m.\nPublic $20\, TBG Members $15 (plus applicable taxes and fees)\n\n\nPrevious Sessions: \n\nSession 1: Native Plant Series: Collecting Native Seed – Saturday\, October 25\, 2025\nSession 2: Native Plant Series: Winter Sowing – Saturday\, January 10\, 2026\n\nAbout Tina Cesaroni & Pat Concessi\nToronto Master Gardeners\, Tina and Pat\, are transitioning their home gardens to more natural environments\, which includes adding native plants\, shrubs and trees. They collect seed each fall and grow native plants from seed for their own gardens and to share with the their communities. \nAbout Toronto Master Gardeners\nToronto Master Gardeners (TMG) is a volunteer not-for-profit organization that shares current\, science-based horticultural information with the gardening public through various channels\, including in person\, in print\, through the media\, and online. Our committed volunteers support and inspire the community\, and continually update the sound knowledge required to help them. Learn more and ask your questions Toronto Master Gardeners – Helping Gardeners. \nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden\nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member! \nAdditional Program Information\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program please email programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/native-plant-series-potting-up-seedlings-plant-exchange/
LOCATION:Toronto Botanical Garden\, 777 Lawrence Ave E\, Toronto\, ON\, M3C 1P2\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Gardening
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/fc04d404012287673605e8a93de7a47c.jpg
END:VEVENT
