X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69d6dcae129f12743837691b"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:NatureTO: Trees Around the Branch Tour
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260608T180000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260608T193000Z
UID:69d6dcae129f12743837691b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Barbara Frum library and its neighbourhood is home to a va
 riety of trees. Join the City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff to explore t
 he natural world on a local neighbourhood tour. Learn how to recognize dif
 ferent species and fun facts about their cultural and ecological importanc
 e.\nChildren under 12 must be accompanied by a parent/caregiver.\nRegistra
 tion is required.\nThe tour will start and end at the Barbara Frum library
 \, outside the front doors\, and will be guided by the City of Toronto Urb
 an Forestry staff. There may be uneven\, unpaved surfaces along the route.
  Please dress and prepare accordingly for this outdoor program (e.g. glove
 s/mittens\, hats\, sunscreen\, water\, comfortable shoes). This program ta
 kes place rain or shine. In the event of severe inclement weather\, regist
 rants will be notified of an alternative date.\nInformation Collection Not
 ice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Pu
 blic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and
  20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registrati
 on\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your
  information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\,
  416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Barbara Frum\, Begins outside the library's front doors.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69d6dcae129f12743837691b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
