BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup: Toronto Enterprise DevOps": "https://www.meetup.com/toronto-enterprise-devops-user-group/events/313910537/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_devops
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Toronto Enterprise DevOps
UID:event_313910537@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260411T140324Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260611T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260611T193000
SUMMARY:Vibe Coding the Platform: Agentic DevOps with Claude Code & Codex
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Enterprise DevOps User Group\nLLM chat was the warm-up
 .\n\nAsk a question. Copy. Paste. Tweak.\nUseful — but capped.\n\nThe re
 al shift is agentic DevOps workflows using tools like Claude Code and the 
 OpenAI Codex App — systems that can reason across repositories\, plan mu
 lti-step changes\, modify infrastructure\, and operate closer to how real 
 engineers build.\n\nThis session is both 101 and 201.\n\nIf you’re new t
 o agentic tooling\, you’ll understand what’s fundamentally different f
 rom chat-based usage.\nIf you’re already experimenting\, you’ll leave 
 with practical agentic patterns for workflow design\, context control\, in
 frastructure changes\, and avoiding unstructured vibe coding.\n\nNot using
  agentic tooling in DevOps today is starting to feel like refusing to use 
 the internet in 2003.\n\nThis isn’t about hype.\nIt’s about leverage.\
 n\nIt’s a great time to be a builder — if you build with agents.\n\n*C
 ome at 5:30 pm have some pizza and chat for a bit. The presentation starts
  at 6:00 pm.*
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/toronto-enterprise-devops-user-group/
 events/313910537/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260323T143404Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260323T143404Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
