BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"City of Toronto Festivals & Events": "www.jimbravopaintings.weebly.com"}
X-SOURCE-ID:toronto_festivals
SUMMARY:Los Callejeros Exhibition
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260618T100000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260723T100000
UID:2e4118eb01b3554b2f4e16f475f2e661@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:Explore selections from works reflecting Jim Bravo’s memorie
 s of his early immigrant inner-city experiences\, and correlated interpret
 ations of our sublime Canadian landscape. This exhibition adds yet another
  voice to the developing story and renewed global interest surrounding que
 stions of race and immigration witnessed in society recently. \n\nAbout th
 e Artist \nJim Bravo was born in Ecuador\, South America\, and is of Afro-
 Latino and Quichua descent. He emigrated to Toronto Canada with his family
  in the mid 70s and spent his youth in the downtown central west and east 
 core of the city. He is a graduate of The Ontario College of Art and Desig
 n University where he majored in Fine Art and public monumental painting. 
 A multi award winning painter including first honor for the prestigious 20
 23 Kingston Prize For Contemporary Canadian Portraiture\, Bravo is also th
 e recipient of grants from Toronto Art Council\, Ontario Arts Council gran
 ts and TABIA Mural Award. \nCategories: Arts/Exhibits\, Artisan\nFree even
 t
LOCATION:Assembly Hall Gallery\, 1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr\, Etobicok
 e\, ON\, M8V 4B6
URL:www.jimbravopaintings.weebly.com
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
