BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6959368f48a98474cec35940"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Robotics Club
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260626T200000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260626T210000Z
UID:6959368f48a98474cec35940@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the library for a fun hour of robotics and coding. 
 Get creative with Snap Circuits\, Dash and Dot\, Sphero Robots and Scratch
  Jr! For ages\n6-12.\nDue to the limited number of robots\, participants 
 may be asked to share with other participants.
LOCATION:Parliament Street\, Main Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6959368f48a98474cec35940
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6971201c91e4576f847de1df"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Video Game Café
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260626T200000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260626T220000Z
UID:6971201c91e4576f847de1df@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us in the Youth Hub every Friday to play video games on o
 ur Nintendo Switch or PS5 with your friends! Ask us for our list of video 
 games\, and check our monthly calendar for Gaming Tournaments with prizes!
 \nThis program is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming pl
 ace for teens after school and in the summer\, where helpful staff are alw
 ays available. Free\, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a bra
 nch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to find out more.
LOCATION:Eatonville
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6971201c91e4576f847de1df
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b1b16c19c54125aa032411"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Dash & Dot Robotics
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260626T200000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260626T210000Z
UID:69b1b16c19c54125aa032411@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Interested in exploring science\, technology\, engineering and
  math (STEM)? This month we are going to\nlearn coding using Dash and Dot 
 robots! For ages 6-12.\nRegistration is required. Parent/Caregiver must at
 tend.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this fo
 rm is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries A
 ct\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used
  for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions a
 bout how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerlin
 e staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toront
 o ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Spadina Road\, Children's Area
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b1b16c19c54125aa032411
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69612a7f6f926136000f4251"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69603a014a9fd98b7f76754a"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:After School Club
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260626T200000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260626T210000Z
UID:69603a014a9fd98b7f76754a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Looking for something to do after school? Come out to our Afte
 r School Club and learn new things\, make stuff\, meet other kids and have
  fun! For ages\n6-12.\nSnacks are offered during the After School Club for
  participants. Ingredient lists will be available. Snacks are generously s
 upported\, in part\, by donors.
LOCATION:St. Clair/Silverthorn\, This program takes place in the upstairs 
 program room.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69603a014a9fd98b7f76754a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
