SUMMARY:Toronto Swahili Summer Festival
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260711T090000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260711T090000
UID:3b45427b8d55c2f8f3c73046a6726746@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:An annual cultural event that celebrates the Swahili language 
 and the diverse heritage of East African communities. The festival is orga
 nized by the Swahili Cultural Centre and provides a platform for people to
  experience Swahili culture through music\, food\, fashion\, art and more.
 \n\nCategories: Cultural\, Food/Culinary\, Live Performances\nFree event
LOCATION:163 Queens Street Wast\, 163 Queen St E\, Toronto\, ON\, M7A 2H6
URL:https://swahiliculturalcenter.com/
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"City of Toronto Festivals & Events": "www.iharpfest.com"}
X-SOURCE-ID:toronto_festivals
SUMMARY:iHarpFest 2026 Toronto International Harp Festival
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260711T093000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260712T100000
UID:59e26e18ab6c1255012099e8eb641048@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:World heritage. Canada’s harmony.\n\nExperience a week of a 
 global gathering of harpists\, educators\, and music lovers celebrating th
 e harp’s timeless beauty and boundless future.\n\nWe're bathering the wo
 rld’s most distinguished harpists together at two of Toronto’s most in
 spiring venues\, the Aga Khan Museum and The Ismaili Centre  for a celebra
 tion of culture\, creativity\, and connection.\n\nFrom Queen Victoria to B
 roadway settings\, from ancient strings to contemporary sounds\, Toronto w
 ill be transformed into the most diverse international stage for the harp\
 , the world’s most ethereal instrument.\nCategories: Live Performances\,
  Music\, Theatre
LOCATION:The Ismaili Center Toronto - Social Hall\, 49 Wynford Dr\, Toront
