X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup: Sci Fi Book Club": "https://www.meetup.com/thescifibookclub/events/312950533/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_scifi_books
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Sci Fi Book Club
UID:event_312950533@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260411T140320Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260726T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260726T160000
SUMMARY:I Who Have Never Known Men - Jacqueline Harpman
DESCRIPTION:The Sci Fi Book Club\nHi everyone\,\n\nOur selection for July 
 is short but mighty story\, and I'm here for it. It has been rediscovered 
 recently on BookTok and is being compared to books like Margaret Atwood’
 s *A Handmaid's Tale* and Octavia E Butler’s *Parable* series. Translate
 d from French and published in 1995 then slipped into relative obscurity. 
 The themes are intense but I'm told that the storytelling and the message 
 are well worth it. If you're interested in learning more about the book's 
 resurgence\, check out this great [Guardian article](https://www.theguardi
 an.com/books/2025/feb/01/i-who-have-never-known-men-lost-dystopia-new-read
 ers-after-buzz-on-tiktok).\n\nBook of the Month\n*I Who Have Never Known M
 en* \\- Jacqueline Harpman \\(1995\\)\n\nFrom Goodreads\, *I Who Have Neve
 r Known Men* is a story about a group of women imprisoned and guarded. The
  women have no memory of how they got there\, no notion of time\, and only
  a vague recollection of their lives before. What comes next is a story of
  a young woman's fight to uncover her past and make her own future. People
  are divided on the story's finer points\, but just about everyone I've re
 ad has echoed [What Is Quinn Reading](https://www.whatisquinnreading.com/r
 eviews/i-who-have-never-known-men-book-review)'s review\, saying they're g
 rateful for the read and will carry it with them. At approximately 190 pag
 es\, I'm glad you'all feel that we should dive in and investigate this kin
 d of story.\n\nTo join a Book Club meeting\, all you will need is YOURSELF
 . If you haven’t had a chance to finish the book\, we still would love f
 or you to join us in the discussion.\n\nNot able to join us in person for 
 events? [The Sci Fi Book Club is on Discord](https://discord.gg/B9NMnC2F).
  Join us and keep the conversation going.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/thescifibookclub/events/312950533/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260119T014750Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260119T014750Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
