X-SOURCE-ID:toronto_festivals
SUMMARY:How to Survive a Bear Attack by Claire Cameron - By the Lake Book 
 Club
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260915T190000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260915T190000
UID:2f02cbbbe586396d614f9fc67eac3ea6@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:How to Survive a Bear Attack\, by Claire Cameron\, finalist fo
 r the 2025 Governor General’s Literary Award in Non-Fiction\, investigat
 es a rare bear attack in Algonquin Park while reflecting on her own battle
  with genetic cancer. Blending nature writing\, true crime and memoir\, Ca
 meron explores fear\, resilience and survival.\n\nBy the Lake Book Club ho
 sts six Tuesday-night events from February to December with top Canadian a
 uthors and Humber Polytechnics alumni. Each in-person event features readi
 ngs\, discussions\, Q&A\, book signings and ASL interpretation\, while vir
 tual sessions include live subtitles and audio access.\nCategories: Litera
 ry
LOCATION:Assembly Hall\, 1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr\, Etobicoke\, ON\,
  M8V 4B6
URL:https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-cent
 res-galleries/assembly-hall/
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"City of Toronto Festivals & Events": "https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/assembly-hall/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:toronto_festivals
SUMMARY:By the Lake Book Club – 3-Event Package
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260915T190000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260915T190000
UID:b6560fd6e42887687094288c7882b146@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy the final three By the Lake Book Club events of 2026 for
  just $55. Join Humber Polytechnic alumni as they dive into conversation w
 ith leading Canadian authors. This package features Claire Cameron\, Emma 
 Knight and Anne Michaels. Each event includes a reading\, discussion\, aud
 ience Q&A\, book-signing and American sign language interpretation.\n\nBy 
 the Lake Book Club hosts six Tuesday-night events from February to Decembe
 r with top Canadian authors and Humber Polytechnics alumni. Each in-person
  event features readings\, discussions\, Q&A\, book signings and ASL inter
 pretation\, while virtual sessions include live subtitles and audio access
 .\n\nClaire Cameron - September 15\, 2026 at 7 p.m.\nEmma Knight - October
  6\, 2026 at 7 p.m.\nAnne Michaels - December 8\, 2026 at 7 p.m.\n\nCatego
 ries: Literary\nPrice: 55.00
LOCATION:Assembly Hall \, 1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr\, Etobicoke\, ON\
 , M8V 4B6
URL:https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-cent
 res-galleries/assembly-hall/
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
