DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260921T220000Z
UID:69a9cc1719c54125aa0282bd@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Brookbanks branch and its neighbourhood is home to a varie
 ty of trees. Join the\nCity of Toronto Urban Forestry\nteam\nto explore th
 e natural world on a local neighbourhood tour. Learn how to recognize diff
 erent species and fun facts about their cultural and ecological importance
 .\nFree program.\nRegistration will open up one month before the program d
 ate. Children under 12 must be accompanied by a parent/caregiver.\nPresen
 ted as part of TPL’s environmental program series\, Our Fragile Planet. 
 The series is generously supported by Friends of Toronto Public Library\, 
 South Chapter.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information o
 n this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Li
 braries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will onl
 y be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Qu
 estions about how the library handles your information can be directed to 
 Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street
 \, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Brookbanks
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a9cc1719c54125aa0282bd
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
