BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"City of Toronto Festivals & Events": "https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/assembly-hall/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:toronto_festivals
SUMMARY:The Life Cycle of the Common Octopus by Emma Knight - By the Lake 
 Book Club 
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261006T190000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261006T190000
UID:e13667695ccae568b1d3436ef58c6a31@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:The Life Cycle of the Common Octopus\, by Emma Knight\, shortl
 isted for the 2025 Scotiabank Giller Prize\, is a spellbinding debut about
  friendship\, motherhood\, first love and the secrets that shape us. Set a
 gainst the moody backdrop of Edinburgh\, the novel follows Pen\, a Canadia
 n student unraveling a family mystery while navigating independence and de
 sire. With wit and emotional depth\, Knight explores womanhood and the cho
 ices that bind us.\n\nBy the Lake Book Club hosts six Tuesday-night events
  from February to December with top Canadian authors and Humber Polytechni
 cs alumni. Each in-person event features readings\, discussions\, Q&A\, bo
 ok signings and ASL interpretation\, while virtual sessions include live s
 ubtitles and audio access.\nCategories: Literary
LOCATION:Assembly Hall\, 1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr\, Etobicoke\, ON\,
  M8V 4B6
URL:https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-cent
 res-galleries/assembly-hall/
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
