BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"City of Toronto Festivals & Events": "daniellecole.ca"}
X-SOURCE-ID:toronto_festivals
SUMMARY:Cowboys and Wallflowers Exhibition
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261008T100000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-05:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261107T100000
UID:824d515a402d872a52f7458631624467@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:Immerse in collages that blend iconic imagery and wit to chall
 enge gender norms and domestic expectations. Despite shifting gender dynam
 ics\, her work highlights ongoing struggles over household roles. Each pie
 ce is meticulously handmade from vintage materials dating 1800s–1970s by
  Danielle Colle. \n\nAbout the Artist\nDanielle Cole is a Toronto-based ar
 tist whose collages\, composed of vintage graphics\, examine domestic role
 s and consumerism. Her work has been exhibited internationally and feature
 d in CBC Arts\, Kolaj Magazine and Toronto Life.\nCategories: Arts/Exhibit
 s\, Artisan\nFree event
LOCATION:Assembly Hall Gallery\, 1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr\, Etobicok
 e\, ON\, M8V 4B6
URL:daniellecole.ca
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
